{"text":"MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "The Breeze feels like a natural next choice after Old Sock because I want more of that relaxed, bluesy Clapton sound.",
    "In My Soul fits the soulful blues mood I associate with Memphis and Old Sock, while Revelator also connects with my interest in expressive guitar playing."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "Shadows in the Night misses what I want today: traditional vocal standards do not satisfy my interest in blues and roots rock.",
    "The mellow songwriting of Before This World and the melodic rock of New appeal to me, but neither gives me as direct a reason to listen now as the two blues choices."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "Recognizing a familiar artist is not enough for me; the particular album needs to fit the sound I want today.",
    "My interest in roots-oriented music seems to have been stretched into treating country, mellow songwriting, and blues as equally compelling next choices."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "The connection between Memphis and Old Sock matters because soulful, relaxed blues is what draws me most strongly on this visit.",
    "An album can fit my taste without prompting me to choose it now; I rarely act on more than the strongest matches."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations understood my broad interest in roots and guitar music, but only some captured the soulful blues sound that makes me want to listen today."
}"}
